    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.visits\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHi echasnovski! Is it possible to extend mini.visits to do something like how https://github.com/otavioschwanck/arrow.nvim does it.\r\nBasically we can press ';' key and then navigate to the top few files using numbers. \r\nI believe this could be achieved using mini.visits altough navigating using numbers is not possible i guess since it uses vim.ui.select.\r\nIs it possible to do something like this or is there a workaround to achieve this.",
